<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Marshall Bartholomew's arrangement</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1930</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jericho Rhapsody (Morton Gould)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1941</span><span class="sg-chain-h">based on the song, for concert band</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Joshua (Ralph Flanagan and His Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1950</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adaptation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">101 Gang Songs (Bing Crosby)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">in a medley</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Songs of My People (Thea Bowman)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Joshua 6:15–21 (the Battle of Jericho)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the story it tells</span></li></ul></section>
